course: dictionary
lesson: 9241
title: Soppy and the feelings behind a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how a writer feels, not just what happens. «Grown-ups call very sweet romantic film scenes "soppy", and children are allowed to look away or roll their eyes.» The clues are the sweet romantic scenes and the eye-rolling. So soppy means too sweet and full of love-talk, in a way that some people find silly.
explain: Soppy can also describe a person. A soppy person is silly, weak or soft-hearted, and gets upset too easily. The word often sounds a little teasing. When someone says, «Don't be soppy!», they are telling you not to make such a big fuss about feelings.
explain: Check a new word by swapping in your meaning. Try "too sweet and sentimental" in place of soppy. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Soppy is an adjective, and it can change to soppier and soppiest.
fact: In everyday British speech, «soppy» means too soft and sentimental, full of love-talk or easy tears.
fact: «Soppy» can also mean silly, weak or soft-hearted, as in «a soppy person».
fact: The word is informal, so you would use it in chatty talk, not in a formal school report.
fact: A rare meaning of «soppy» is very wet and soaked, as in «soppy grass after the rain».
exercise: «Grown-ups call very sweet romantic film scenes "soppy", and children are allowed to look away or roll their eyes.» What does soppy mean here? | Fast and noisy | Very clever and serious | Very wet and soaked through | *Too sweet and full of love-talk, in a way some people find silly
exercise: Ella tells her brother, «Don't be soppy!» What does she mean? | Don't get soaked in the rain | *Don't be so silly and sentimental about feelings | Don't be so loud and fast | Don't be so tall
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes the card: «The soppy card had hearts all over it.» | hearts | over | card | *soppy
test: «That film is so soppy!» What does the speaker think of the film? | It is very funny and fast | It is very scary and dark | *It is too sweet and romantic, and it feels a bit embarrassing | It is very wet and soaked
test: Someone who cries at every card might be called soppy. Which meaning fits best? | Very cold and wet | *Silly, weak or soft-hearted, too easily upset | Very good at sports | Very quick at running
exam: After the storm, the field was soppy and our socks were soaked. Which meaning of soppy is used here? | Too sweet and romantic | *Very wet and soaked | Silly and weak | Too loud and noisy
